meta {
  name: 6. Pay For Request (B)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/requests/{{requestId}}/pay
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Telegram-Init-Data: {{initDataB}}
}

docs {
  Only reachable after "4. Accept Request (A)" — payment always comes
  after acceptance, never before (400 otherwise). Run "2. Dev Top Up
  (B)" (Wallet folder) first, or this returns 402 — the offer's
  price_stars is converted to Toman at the current star_to_toman_rate
  (4,000 by default) and charged against User B's wallet balance.

  Calling this a second time for the same request returns 400 — a
  request can only be paid for once.

  User B is charged the full price immediately. User A's net share
  (gross minus the chat commission — 10% by default, rounded in User
  A's favor) is NOT credited yet, though — the response's "status" is
  "pending", not "succeeded". This is the "idle money" model (see
  TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENTS.md section 10): a chat-request transaction
  only actually pays out once its chat session closes AND the
  chat_release_grace_hours window passes with no dispute — check
  "3./4. Get Balance" (Wallet folder) right after paying and you'll see
  User B's balance drop, but User A's stays flat, with the net share
  showing up in "pending_toman" instead. Contrast with Photos > "5.
  Purchase Photo", which settles instantly.

  This also opens the chat session itself — see the "Chat Sessions"
  folder to close it (and watch the pending share move once the grace
  window passes).
}
